{
  "comprehensible": "The board dealt with the proposal quickly and without much attention, and the CFO was left to take the blame.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "gave the proposal short shrift",
      "gloss": "dealt with the proposal quickly and without giving it much attention or consideration"
    },
    {
      "expression": "carry the can",
      "gloss": "take the blame or responsibility for something that has gone wrong"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "董事会对该提案草草处理，首席财务官只好背黑锅。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "At the very last moment, he lost his nerve and betrayed his colleagues by shifting the blame onto them.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "bottled it",
      "gloss": "lost his nerve and failed to do something at the crucial moment"
    },
    {
      "expression": "threw his colleagues under the bus",
      "gloss": "betrayed his colleagues by sacrificing them to protect himself"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "他在最后一刻临阵退缩，还把同事推出去当替罪羊。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The manager only admitted that someone had changed the figures dishonestly after the auditors had left.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "doctored",
      "gloss": "changed dishonestly to deceive people"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the auditors had gone",
      "gloss": "the official inspectors had left"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The sentence begins with 'Not until...', which makes the main clause ('did the manager admit...') use inverted word order: 'did the manager admit' instead of 'the manager admitted'. This structure emphasizes that the admission happened only after the auditors left.",
  "translation": "直到审计员离开之后，经理才承认数据被篡改了。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The house was in a state of dignified but shabby decline, because the people who lived there had moved away to mainland Europe a long time ago.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "genteel decay",
      "gloss": "a kind of decline that still keeps a respectable, upper-class appearance"
    },
    {
      "expression": "having long since repaired to",
      "gloss": "having moved to (a place) a long time ago"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the Continent",
      "gloss": "mainland Europe (used especially by British speakers)"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The phrase 'its occupants having long since repaired to the Continent' is a participial clause that gives the reason for the house's decay. It does not have a subject-verb agreement with the main clause; instead, 'having repaired' is a perfect participle showing an action completed before the house's state. The subject of this clause is 'its occupants', which is different from the subject of the main clause ('The house').",
  "translation": "这栋房子处于一种体面而衰败的状态，因为它的住户早已移居到欧洲大陆去了。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The results hint at something rather than prove it, and people should not read too much into them.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "suggestive rather than conclusive",
      "gloss": "hinting at a possible answer rather than proving it"
    },
    {
      "expression": "ought not to be over-read",
      "gloss": "should not be interpreted as meaning more than they actually show"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "这些发现只是提示性的，而非结论性的，不应过度解读。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The person renting the property must protect the owner from any claims that come from breaking any of the promises in this agreement.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "indemnify",
      "gloss": "protect someone from loss or damage by paying for it"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessee",
      "gloss": "the person who rents the property"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessor",
      "gloss": "the person who owns the property and rents it out"
    },
    {
      "expression": "covenants herein",
      "gloss": "the promises stated in this document"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "承租人应就因违反本协议中的任何约定而引起的所有索赔，向出租人作出赔偿。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The report does not go as far as to say who is to blame, but the things it suggests are very easy to notice.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "stops short of",
      "gloss": "does not go as far as (doing something); deliberately does not do it"
    },
    {
      "expression": "apportioning blame",
      "gloss": "saying who is responsible for something bad; giving out blame"
    },
    {
      "expression": "hard to miss",
      "gloss": "very easy to notice; impossible not to see"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "这份报告没有走到追究责任那一步，但它所暗示的东西很难让人忽略。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "He was, to say the least, quite unhappy with the result.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "to put it mildly",
      "gloss": "used to say that you are describing something in a gentler way than it deserves; the real situation is stronger"
    },
    {
      "expression": "not best pleased",
      "gloss": "very annoyed or unhappy (a polite, understated way of saying this)"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "说得客气一点，他对这个结果很不满意。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The committee thought it was just an ordinary mistake, but actually the omission was done on purpose, so that the minister would not have to face a difficult question.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "had taken for",
      "gloss": "had thought it was"
    },
    {
      "expression": "routine oversight",
      "gloss": "a normal mistake made by accident"
    },
    {
      "expression": "deliberate omission",
      "gloss": "something left out on purpose"
    },
    {
      "expression": "spare",
      "gloss": "save from having to deal with"
    },
    {
      "expression": "awkward question",
      "gloss": "a difficult or embarrassing question"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The sentence has a contrast: 'What the committee had taken for a routine oversight' is the subject, and 'was in fact a deliberate omission' is the main verb. The phrase 'designed to spare...' describes the omission. The structure may be hard because the subject is a long clause, and the contrast between what seemed and what was is expressed with 'in fact'.",
  "translation": "委员会原以为那只是一次普通的疏忽，但实际上那是有意为之的省略，目的是让部长免于面对一个尴尬的问题。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The company was responsible for paying an amount of money that it could not easily afford.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "on the hook for",
      "gloss": "responsible for paying or dealing with something"
    },
    {
      "expression": "a sum it could ill afford",
      "gloss": "an amount of money that it could not easily pay without difficulty"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "这家公司需要承担一笔它难以负担的款项。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The reaction happens only when a catalyst is there. If there is no catalyst, the activation energy is so high that the reaction cannot take place.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "proceeds",
      "gloss": "happens or goes forward"
    },
    {
      "expression": "in the presence of",
      "gloss": "when something is there"
    },
    {
      "expression": "without which",
      "gloss": "and if it is not there"
    },
    {
      "expression": "prohibitively high",
      "gloss": "so high that it prevents the reaction from happening"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The phrase 'without which' introduces a condition that depends on the preceding noun 'catalyst'. It means 'if the catalyst is not present'. The sentence is a single statement with a main clause and a relative clause; the relative clause is attached to 'catalyst' and explains what happens in its absence.",
  "translation": "该反应只有在催化剂存在时才能进行；如果没有催化剂，活化能会高得使反应无法发生。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "It is proper for us to think about whether acting in that way fits with what we are obliged to do.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "behoves us",
      "gloss": "is right or proper for us"
    },
    {
      "expression": "such a course of action",
      "gloss": "acting in that way"
    },
    {
      "expression": "consonant with",
      "gloss": "in agreement with; fitting with"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "我们应当考虑，这样的做法是否符合我们的义务。"
}
